{"encoding": "verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1", "phase": "prove", "attempt": 1, "request": "Software engineering task A23: Signed arithmetic floor-sum kernel\n\nImplement solution.py with a single solve(data) function. data and the return value must be JSON-compatible. Use Python 3 standard library only; perform no external I/O and do not read benchmark files. All supplied inputs satisfy the stated schema and bounds; no behavior is required for malformed input. Input {n,m,a,b}: 0<=n<=500, m>0, a/b any signed integers (possibly magnitude 10^30). Return exact sum of floor((a*i+b)/m) for i=0..n-1. Floor means toward negative infinity, not truncation. Empty sum is zero; avoid floating point.\n\nImplement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py. Use only the standard library, no external I/O. The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value. Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.\n\nPublic examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"a\": -2, \"b\": 1, \"m\": 3, \"n\": 4}, \"output\": -4}, {\"input\": {\"a\": 100, \"b\": -99, \"m\": 7, \"n\": 0}, \"output\": 0}]\n", "clauses": [{"clause_id": "C1", "quote": "Software engineering task A23: Signed arithmetic floor-sum kernel", "refs": []}, {"clause_id": "C2", "quote": "Implement solution.py with a single solve(data) function.", "refs": ["O2"]}, {"clause_id": "C3", "quote": "data and the return value must be JSON-compatible.", "refs": ["D1"]}, {"clause_id": "C4", "quote": "Use Python 3 standard library only;", "refs": ["S1"]}, {"clause_id": "C5", "quote": "perform no external I/O and do not read benchmark files.", "refs": ["S1"]}, {"clause_id": "C6", "quote": "All supplied inputs satisfy the stated schema and bounds;", "refs": ["A1"]}, {"clause_id": "C7", "quote": "no behavior is required for malformed input.", "refs": ["N1"]}, {"clause_id": "C8", "quote": "Input {n,m,a,b}: 0<=n<=500, m>0, a/b any signed integers (possibly magnitude 10^30).", "refs": ["D1", "A1"]}, {"clause_id": "C9", "quote": "Return exact sum of floor((a*i+b)/m) for i=0..n-1.", "refs": ["O1", "S2"]}, {"clause_id": "C10", "quote": "Floor means toward negative infinity, not truncation.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C11", "quote": "Empty sum is zero;", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C12", "quote": "avoid floating point.", "refs": ["S2"]}, {"clause_id": "C13", "quote": "Implement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py.", "refs": ["O2"]}, {"clause_id": "C14", "quote": "Use only the standard library, no external I/O.", "refs": ["S1"]}, {"clause_id": "C15", "quote": "The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value.", "refs": ["D1"]}, {"clause_id": "C16", "quote": "Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.", "refs": ["D1"]}, {"clause_id": "C17", "quote": "Public examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"a\": -2, \"b\": 1, \"m\": 3, \"n\": 4}, \"output\": -4}, {\"input\": {\"a\": 100, \"b\": -99, \"m\": 7, \"n\": 0}, \"output\": 0}]", "refs": ["O1"]}], "records": [{"id": "D1", "revision": 1, "kind": "entity", "role": "declaration", "statement": "The input is a JSON-compatible object with integer fields n, m, a and b; the output is a JSON-serializable integer.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 175, "interpretation": "JSON compatibility", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 125}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 456, "interpretation": "Input fields and integer domain", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 372}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 802, "interpretation": "JSON input and serializable output", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 729}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 868, "interpretation": "Preserve specified structure and ordering; the scalar result has no collection ordering", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 803}], "scope": ["solve input and output"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["The input structure is {n,m,a,b}.", "The returned value is a scalar integer, preserving the specified output structure."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:fb26af82c2f9a12e61a240a545ac8b524457c1945e9809ce547f4b157d03dc7f", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "A1", "revision": 1, "kind": "precondition", "role": "assumption", "statement": "Supplied inputs satisfy the schema: integer n with 0<=n<=500, positive integer m, and signed integer a and b, including magnitudes of 10^30.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 326, "interpretation": "Explicit supplied-input validity assumption", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 269}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 456, "interpretation": "Schema and bounds", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 372}], "scope": ["supplied inputs"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Every supplied input has the stated fields and integer types.", "0<=n<=500 and m>0.", "Signed a and b are supported without imposing a smaller magnitude limit."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:2a1b54317ed09f6a8680bfe964dedfa9f05b2a0dfca848ab9d83b9e8c3def6ba", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O1", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "For every supplied valid input, return the exact integer sum of floor((a*i+b)/m) over i from 0 through n-1, with floor toward negative infinity and the empty sum equal to zero.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 507, "interpretation": "Exact floor-sum result", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 457}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 561, "interpretation": "Signed floor semantics", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 508}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 580, "interpretation": "Empty-sum behavior", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 562}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1052, "interpretation": "Required public examples and applicability to held-out valid inputs", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 870}], "scope": ["all inputs satisfying A1"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "A1", "relation": "assumes"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["The result equals the mathematical floor sum for every valid input.", "Negative quotients are rounded toward negative infinity, never truncated toward zero.", "n=0 returns 0.", "Input {a:-2,b:1,m:3,n:4} returns -4.", "Input {a:100,b:-99,m:7,n:0} returns 0."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:4dcf7092df3733835a14ad966404cf7b73751d0d50a1092510ae369c4694b3ea", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O2", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Implement solution.py exposing a single pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data).", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 124, "interpretation": "File and single-function interface", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 67}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 680, "interpretation": "Python 3, purity and determinism", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 604}], "scope": ["solution.py and solve(data)"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["solution.py provides the single requested solve(data) function.", "Identical input values yield identical returned values.", "The function does not mutate its input or depend on mutable external state."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:7be0e1f2b6afb5d52916871d2cf1c0536bc19281065af4f60345e22d99703f5c", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "S1", "revision": 1, "kind": "safety_property", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Use only the Python 3 standard library, perform no external I/O, and never read benchmark files.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 211, "interpretation": "Standard-library restriction", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 176}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 268, "interpretation": "External I/O and benchmark-reading prohibition", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 212}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 728, "interpretation": "Repeated library and I/O restrictions", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 681}], "scope": ["implementation and execution"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["No third-party libraries are required.", "Execution performs no external I/O.", "Benchmark files are never read."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:b05b54ceedb5f5f578e713f2c933fb7d4cb99e85b1b36cf3412cce35fc02ca09", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "S2", "revision": 1, "kind": "safety_property", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Compute the floor sum using exact integer arithmetic without floating point.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 602, "interpretation": "Floating-point prohibition", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 581}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 507, "interpretation": "Exact numerical result", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 457}], "scope": ["all arithmetic used to compute the result"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["No floating-point conversion or arithmetic is used in the computation.", "Large signed values retain exact precision."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:6bbc9eeeabf85b5a1de02ad1f7caac856cd2af88cd06398e082e864ac0056002", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "N1", "revision": 1, "kind": "explicit_non_goal", "role": "exclusion", "statement": "Behavior for malformed inputs is outside the required scope.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd", "document_ref": "tasks/A23/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 371, "interpretation": "Explicit malformed-input exclusion", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 327}], "scope": ["inputs violating the stated schema or bounds"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["No validation, error response or numerical result is required for malformed inputs."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:628c93fb15c6ff2582ff714f3f48e1b284ef5ad1b7f37b1e173d8ba4a6fe428f", "blocked_by": []}], "lean_source": "import Std\n\n-- BEGIN VERISLOP REGISTRY\n-- Generated by `verislop formalize`. Typed obligation metadata: an index, never evidence.\nnamespace VeriSlop.Registry\n\nstructure SourceRef where\n  documentRef : String\n  documentHash : String\n  startByte : Nat\n  endByte : Nat\n  origin : String\n  interpretation : String\n\nstructure Dependency where\n  id : String\n  relation : String\n\nstructure Entry where\n  id : String\n  revision : Nat\n  kind : String\n  role : String\n  statement : String\n  required : Bool\n  sourceRefs : List SourceRef\n  scope : List String\n  dependencies : List Dependency\n  acceptanceCriteria : List String\n  bindings : List String\n\ndef «D1» : Entry := {\n  id := \"D1\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"entity\",\n  role := \"declaration\",\n  statement := \"The input is a JSON-compatible object with integer fields n, m, a and b; the output is a JSON-serializable integer.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 125, endByte := 175, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"JSON compatibility\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 372, endByte := 456, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Input fields and integer domain\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 729, endByte := 802, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"JSON input and serializable output\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 803, endByte := 868, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Preserve specified structure and ordering; the scalar result has no collection ordering\" }],\n  scope := [\"solve input and output\"],\n  dependencies := [],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"The input structure is {n,m,a,b}.\", \"The returned value is a scalar integer, preserving the specified output structure.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.Input\", \"VeriSlopAST.solve\"] }\n\ndef «A1» : Entry := {\n  id := \"A1\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"precondition\",\n  role := \"assumption\",\n  statement := \"Supplied inputs satisfy the schema: integer n with 0<=n<=500, positive integer m, and signed integer a and b, including magnitudes of 10^30.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 269, endByte := 326, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Explicit supplied-input validity assumption\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 372, endByte := 456, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Schema and bounds\" }],\n  scope := [\"supplied inputs\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"D1\", relation := \"uses_definition\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"Every supplied input has the stated fields and integer types.\", \"0<=n<=500 and m>0.\", \"Signed a and b are supported without imposing a smaller magnitude limit.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.valid_input\"] }\n\ndef «O1» : Entry := {\n  id := \"O1\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"postcondition\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"For every supplied valid input, return the exact integer sum of floor((a*i+b)/m) over i from 0 through n-1, with floor toward negative infinity and the empty sum equal to zero.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 457, endByte := 507, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Exact floor-sum result\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 508, endByte := 561, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Signed floor semantics\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 562, endByte := 580, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Empty-sum behavior\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 870, endByte := 1052, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Required public examples and applicability to held-out valid inputs\" }],\n  scope := [\"all inputs satisfying A1\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"D1\", relation := \"uses_definition\" }, { id := \"A1\", relation := \"assumes\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"The result equals the mathematical floor sum for every valid input.\", \"Negative quotients are rounded toward negative infinity, never truncated toward zero.\", \"n=0 returns 0.\", \"Input {a:-2,b:1,m:3,n:4} returns -4.\", \"Input {a:100,b:-99,m:7,n:0} returns 0.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.floor_sum_correct\"] }\n\ndef «O2» : Entry := {\n  id := \"O2\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"postcondition\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"Implement solution.py exposing a single pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data).\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 67, endByte := 124, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"File and single-function interface\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 604, endByte := 680, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Python 3, purity and determinism\" }],\n  scope := [\"solution.py and solve(data)\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"D1\", relation := \"uses_definition\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"solution.py provides the single requested solve(data) function.\", \"Identical input values yield identical returned values.\", \"The function does not mutate its input or depend on mutable external state.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.python_entry\"] }\n\ndef «S1» : Entry := {\n  id := \"S1\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"safety_property\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"Use only the Python 3 standard library, perform no external I/O, and never read benchmark files.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 176, endByte := 211, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Standard-library restriction\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 212, endByte := 268, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"External I/O and benchmark-reading prohibition\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 681, endByte := 728, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Repeated library and I/O restrictions\" }],\n  scope := [\"implementation and execution\"],\n  dependencies := [],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"No third-party libraries are required.\", \"Execution performs no external I/O.\", \"Benchmark files are never read.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.runtime_safety\"] }\n\ndef «S2» : Entry := {\n  id := \"S2\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"safety_property\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"Compute the floor sum using exact integer arithmetic without floating point.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 581, endByte := 602, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Floating-point prohibition\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 457, endByte := 507, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Exact numerical result\" }],\n  scope := [\"all arithmetic used to compute the result\"],\n  dependencies := [],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"No floating-point conversion or arithmetic is used in the computation.\", \"Large signed values retain exact precision.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.integer_arithmetic\"] }\n\ndef «N1» : Entry := {\n  id := \"N1\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"explicit_non_goal\",\n  role := \"exclusion\",\n  statement := \"Behavior for malformed inputs is outside the required scope.\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 327, endByte := 371, origin := \"explicit\", interpretation := \"Explicit malformed-input exclusion\" }],\n  scope := [\"inputs violating the stated schema or bounds\"],\n  dependencies := [],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"No validation, error response or numerical result is required for malformed inputs.\"],\n  bindings := [] }\n\ndef «valid_schema_witness» : Entry := {\n  id := \"valid_schema_witness\",\n  revision := 1,\n  kind := \"non_vacuity\",\n  role := \"guarantee\",\n  statement := \"Non-vacuity: The input with n zero, m one, a zero and b zero satisfies the actual valid_input predicate. (witnesses A1)\",\n  required := true,\n  sourceRefs := [{ documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 269, endByte := 326, origin := \"inferred\", interpretation := \"derived by registered rule verislop.non-vacuity/0.1 from assumption A1\" }, { documentRef := \"tasks/A23/prompt.txt\", documentHash := \"sha256:4210b881ec112b3ceaf86658d8a931f6d4dea05689a85d3e7e72aed9da3911dd\", startByte := 372, endByte := 456, origin := \"inferred\", interpretation := \"derived by registered rule verislop.non-vacuity/0.1 from assumption A1\" }],\n  scope := [\"supplied inputs\"],\n  dependencies := [{ id := \"A1\", relation := \"uses_definition\" }],\n  acceptanceCriteria := [\"Prove the existential theorem with concrete witnesses extractable by bounded kernel head-normalisation.\"],\n  bindings := [\"VeriSlopAST.valid_input_inhabited\"] }\n\ndef entries : List Entry := [«D1», «A1», «O1», «O2», «S1», «S2», «N1», «valid_schema_witness»]\n\nend VeriSlop.Registry\n-- END VERISLOP REGISTRY\n\n/-!\nNormative native boundary fact model, v0.2. The host Python AST-to-fact mapping\nis source-bound and TRUSTED at Tier 0. These theorems prove rules about the fact\nmodel; they do not prove the parser, CPython, ownership analysis or arbitrary\nfuture Python programs. Facts are computed by the registered source checker,\nnever supplied as observations by a candidate author.\n-/\nnamespace VeriSlop.Native\n\ninductive NativeRequirement where\n  | entry (file qualname : String) (arity : Nat)\n  | pureJson\n  | standardRuntimeOnly\n  | noExternalIO\n  | inputPreserved\n  | deterministic\n  | noFloatingPoint\n  deriving DecidableEq\n\nstructure Entry where\n  file : String\n  qualname : String\n  arity : Nat\n  deriving DecidableEq\n\nstructure ModuleFacts where\n  entries : List Entry\n  uniqueFunctions : Bool\n  closedNames : Bool\n  acyclicCalls : Bool\n  pureJson : Bool\n  standardRuntimeOnly : Bool\n  noExternalIO : Bool\n  inputPreserved : Bool\n  deterministic : Bool\n  noFloatingPoint : Bool\n\ndef checkRequirement (r : NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) : Bool :=\n  match r with\n  | .entry f n a => m.uniqueFunctions && decide (Entry.mk f n a ∈ m.entries)\n  | .pureJson => m.closedNames && m.acyclicCalls && m.pureJson\n  | .standardRuntimeOnly => m.standardRuntimeOnly\n  | .noExternalIO => m.noExternalIO\n  | .inputPreserved => m.inputPreserved\n  | .deterministic => m.deterministic\n  | .noFloatingPoint => m.noFloatingPoint\n\ndef HoldsRequirement (r : NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) : Prop :=\n  match r with\n  | .entry f n a => m.uniqueFunctions = true ∧ Entry.mk f n a ∈ m.entries\n  | .pureJson => m.closedNames = true ∧ m.acyclicCalls = true ∧ m.pureJson = true\n  | .standardRuntimeOnly => m.standardRuntimeOnly = true\n  | .noExternalIO => m.noExternalIO = true\n  | .inputPreserved => m.inputPreserved = true\n  | .deterministic => m.deterministic = true\n  | .noFloatingPoint => m.noFloatingPoint = true\n\ndef checkBoundary (rs : List NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) : Bool :=\n  rs.all (fun r => checkRequirement r m)\n\ndef HoldsBoundary (rs : List NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) : Prop :=\n  ∀ r ∈ rs, HoldsRequirement r m\n\ndef Transfer (rs : List NativeRequirement) : Prop :=\n  ∀ m, checkBoundary rs m = true → HoldsBoundary rs m\n\ndef AdmissionInhabited (rs : List NativeRequirement) : Prop :=\n  ∃ m, checkBoundary rs m = true\n\n-- The endpoint is real closed Lean data containing the accepted function.\n-- Its identity is reified and linked independently; the boundary theorem does\n-- not establish functional equivalence to this reference implementation.\nstructure NativeDefinition (τ : Type) where\n  endpoint : τ\n  requirements : List NativeRequirement\n\ndef Contract {τ : Type} (d : NativeDefinition τ) : Prop :=\n  Transfer d.requirements ∧ AdmissionInhabited d.requirements\n\ntheorem checkRequirement_sound (r : NativeRequirement) (m : ModuleFacts) :\n    checkRequirement r m = true → HoldsRequirement r m := by\n  cases r <;> simp [checkRequirement, HoldsRequirement, Bool.and_eq_true] <;> grind\n\ntheorem transfer_sound (rs : List NativeRequirement) : Transfer rs := by\n  intro m h r hr\n  exact checkRequirement_sound r m ((List.all_eq_true.mp h) r hr)\n\ndef witnessEntries : List NativeRequirement → List Entry\n  | [] => []\n  | .entry f n a :: rs => Entry.mk f n a :: witnessEntries rs\n  | _ :: rs => witnessEntries rs\n\ndef modelWitness (rs : List NativeRequirement) : ModuleFacts :=\n  ⟨witnessEntries rs, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true, true⟩\n\ntheorem entry_in_witness (f n : String) (a : Nat) (rs : List NativeRequirement)\n    (h : NativeRequirement.entry f n a ∈ rs) : Entry.mk f n a ∈ witnessEntries rs := by\n  induction rs with\n  | nil => simp at h\n  | cons r rs ih => cases r <;> simp_all [witnessEntries] <;> grind\n\ntheorem admission_inhabited (rs : List NativeRequirement) : AdmissionInhabited rs := by\n  refine ⟨modelWitness rs, List.all_eq_true.mpr ?_⟩\n  intro r hr\n  cases r with\n  | entry f n a =>\n    simp [checkRequirement, modelWitness, entry_in_witness f n a rs hr]\n  | pureJson => rfl\n  | standardRuntimeOnly => rfl\n  | noExternalIO => rfl\n  | inputPreserved => rfl\n  | deterministic => rfl\n  | noFloatingPoint => rfl\n\ntheorem contract_sound {τ : Type} (d : NativeDefinition τ) : Contract d :=\n  ⟨transfer_sound d.requirements, admission_inhabited d.requirements⟩\n\nend VeriSlop.Native\n\nnamespace VeriSlopAST\nstructure «Input» where\n  «n» : _root_.Int\n  «m» : _root_.Int\n  «a» : _root_.Int\n  «b» : _root_.Int\ndef «solve» («_v0» : _root_.VeriSlopAST.«Input») : _root_.Int := (_root_.List.sum (@_root_.List.map _root_.Nat _root_.Int (fun («_v1» : _root_.Nat) => (_root_.Int.fdiv (_root_.Int.add (_root_.Int.mul (_root_.VeriSlopAST.«Input».«a» «_v0») (_root_.Int.ofNat «_v1»)) (_root_.VeriSlopAST.«Input».«b» «_v0»)) (_root_.VeriSlopAST.«Input».«m» «_v0»))) (_root_.List.range (_root_.Int.toNat (_root_.VeriSlopAST.«Input».«n» «